  "body": "Follow-up from the delta review of PR #3026 (comment 7050606760).\n\nThe flat branch of the rotary contour (`lean < LEAN_MIN` in `crates/motion/src/multiaxis/rotary.rs`) fits rings about any horizontal axis. A bar that lies along world Y thus gets rings about Y. No test shows what a machine whose only rotary turns about X does with such a program.\n\nBy reading the code, the program is refused by name in two places:\n- At generation: `rotary_gate::rotary_letter` refuses an axis with \"states no rotary on that line\", if the machine states its axis vectors.\n- At post: `judge::pose_problems` refuses with \"cannot reach that pose\" or \"states no B axis\", and `posting.rs` blocks the post.\n\nBoth checks are older code. No test covers this case.\n\nWork:\n1. Add a test that generates a rotary contour on a bar along world Y for a machine with only an A axis about X.\n2. Assert the refusal by name at generation, or at post. Assert that no NC file is written.\n",
